  {
    "id": "EQ2-06",
    "question": "What steps are required before approving a high-risk vendor that handles personal data and transfers it outside the EEA?",
    "top_score": 0.5577913975,
    "top_vector_score": 0.568273425,
    "top_keyword_score": 0.5333333333333333,
    "top_section": "THIRD-PARTY VENDOR MANAGEMENT",
    "retrieval_seconds": 0.4011317050026264,
    "answer_seconds": 3.883983106992673,
    "total_seconds": 4.285136881007929,
    "answer": "Under **Third-Party Vendor Management**, the required approval process is:\n\n1. The business owner submits a Vendor Request Form in ServiceNow.\n2. Procurement reviews commercial terms and pricing, including SLA, insurance, and liability.\n3. Security conducts a standardized security assessment based on SIG Lite or CAIQ, depending on criticality.\n4. Legal reviews the data processing agreement (DPA) and contract terms.\n5. The DPO reviews and approves the DPA because the vendor handles personal data.\n6. The CISO signs off because the vendor is classified as High risk.\n7. After approval, the vendor is onboarded and added to the Approved Vendor Registry.\n\nUnder **Data Privacy and GDPR Compliance**, the transfer outside the EEA must use an approved mechanism\u2014SCCs, an adequacy decision, or BCRs\u2014and must also be approved by the DPO at dpo@acme.com.",
